WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.589
You may have asked yourself at some
point using Git 'how do I undo that last

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:08.820
commit?' We've talked about how a
commit has a commit ID and that it's

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.900
really important because of the metadata
that includes. Now let's talk about some

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.330
ways that you can undo commits and
especially which ways are the safest. My

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:23.880
best suggestion for changing a commit
in any way is to use 'git revert'. Now, when

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.689
you revert you're not technically
undoing the commit you're actually

00:00:27.689 --> 00:00:32.700
creating a new commit with the exact
opposite changes of whichever commit

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.110
you'd like to undo. This means the
commit ID remains unchanged so it's

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.040
absolutely safe to do even on commits
that you already pushed to the remote

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.960
repository. There's other ways that you
can undo commits too, but you need to be a

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.129
little bit more careful about how you do
them and if you're actually using these

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:56.129
commands on public commits, commits that are on the remote repository. 'git reset'

00:00:56.129 --> 00:01:00.960
is a very popular way to do it and in a
lot of use cases is the best way. Now,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.780
maybe not so much to undo history but to
change the words that you use in a

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:11.580
commit message is 'commit --amend'. 'git
cherry-pick' doesn't so much

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:16.320
undo a commit but it's important to know
that it does actually change that

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.450
commit ID. So, to recap: if you want to
undo a commit 'git revert' is the best way

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.530
to go there are other options, but always
be cognizant if you're changing a

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.740
committee ID if that commit is on the
remote repository.

